%% ARA — Resume Analysis Pipeline Workflow
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as Candidate / Recruiter
  participant Web as Next.js Web App
  participant API as FastAPI Gateway
  participant S3 as MinIO / S3 Storage
  participant Queue as Redis (ARQ Queue)
  participant Worker as ARQ Analysis Worker
  participant DB as PostgreSQL 18
  participant LLM as LLM Engine (Ollama)

  User->>Web: 1. Drop Resume (PDF/DOCX)
  Web->>API: 2. POST /api/v1/resumes/upload-url
  API-->>Web: 3. Return Presigned S3 Upload URL
  Web->>S3: 4. Direct Upload Binary to Storage
  Web->>API: 5. POST /api/v1/resumes/ (Confirm Metadata)
  API->>DB: 6. Insert Record (tenant organization_id)
  Web->>API: 7. POST /api/v1/analysis/jobs (Trigger Analysis)
  API->>DB: 8. Insert Job (status: pending)
  API->>Queue: 9. Enqueue Task (job_id, storage_key)
  API-->>Web: 10. Return 202 Accepted (job_id)
  
  Queue->>Worker: 11. Dequeue Analysis Task
  Worker->>DB: 12. Update Status -> processing
  Worker->>S3: 13. Download & Parse Text
  Worker->>LLM: 14. Prompt for Structured Skill & Gap Extraction
  LLM-->>Worker: 15. Return Structured JSON Result
  Worker->>DB: 16. Store Analysis JSON & Update Status -> completed
  
  loop Polling
    Web->>API: 17. GET /api/v1/analysis/jobs/{job_id}
    API->>DB: 18. Query Job Status
    API-->>Web: 19. Return Completed Analysis Result
  end
  Web-->>User: 20. Render Structured Feedback & ATS Scoring
